# For platforms without systemd. Install with `crontab -e` (per-user) or as a
# file under /etc/cron.d/ (system-wide; that form needs a user column between
# the schedule and the command, e.g. "* * * * * root /usr/local/bin/aub ...").
#
# Runs `aub sample --due` once a minute; `aub` itself decides which configured
# accounts are actually owed a request, so the tick only needs to be shorter
# than the shortest configured sampling interval. See docs/scheduling.md.
#
# cron mails stdout by default, and a healthy tick prints one line per due
# account every run; redirect it so a quiet cadence does not fill a mailbox.
# stderr is left alone: it carries aub's own diagnostic log.
* * * * * /usr/local/bin/aub sample --due >/dev/null
